@database noC-WHO Documentation
******************************************************************************
@NODE MAIN "FR Version 1.30 Complete Guide - by nocTurne deSign/MST in '94"


            @{b}FR (Files-Reverse) - The /X Reverse File Lister V1.3@{ub}
                         (C)1994 nocTurne deSign/MST                     
              -------------------------------------------------
              @{" Overview       " LINK OVER   } General Description of Features
              @{" Installation   " LINK INSTALL} Installing/Configuring FR
              @{" Usage          " LINK USAGE  } Door Usage/Theory
              @{" Changes        " LINK CHANGES} History of Implementation
              @{" Credits/Greets " LINK CREDS  } Where to reach me/Messages
              -------------------------------------------------
         (Users of V1.0-1.2 need only to read the 'Changes' section)

@ENDNODE
*******************************************************************************
@NODE OVER "Files-Reverse V1.3 - Overview"

 FR  allows users to view a file listing in its reverse order, ie the newer
 descriptions  are  outputted  first.    It  should be of value to users of
 relatively  competitive  boards, where the newest uploads of the day are a
 priority.  This door works under AmiExpress 2.x-3.x and Sigma Express.

@ENDNODE
*******************************************************************************
@NODE INSTALL "Files-Reverse V1.3 - Installation"

 This program is an XIM and should be installed as such.  Knowledge of door
 installation is assumed.  Icons have been provided for 3.x owners.

               @{b}"FR.x" Icon ToolTypes Available in Version 1.3@{ub}
               ----------------------------------------------
               @{" Dividers      " LINK TT1} Set Divider Lines as Default
               @{" Colors        " LINK TT2} Set Color Display as Default   
               @{" ShowNewDate   " LINK TT3} Set Date Line as Default   
               @{" FileNumbers   " LINK TT4} Set File Numbering as Default
               @{" NocWhoCompat  " LINK TT5} Make Compatible with noC-WHO    
               @{" Nuker         " LINK TT6} Nuke Door's Name 
               @{" NukeAccess    " LINK TT7} Access Required to Nuke
               @{" LowMemory     " LINK TT8} Engage Low Memory Mode Always
               ----------------------------------------------
@ENDNODE
******************************************************************************
@NODE TT1 "Files-Reverse V1.3 Icon ToolType - Dividers"

 @{b}Template: @{ub}Dividers=[YES/NO]
  @{b}Example: @{ub}Dividers=YES 

 If you want to enable by default the dividing lines between each filename,
 simply  set  this  tooltype  to  YES.    The  text in "FR-Div.txt" will be
 utilized as the divider graphic.  Please keep the file ONE line long, with
 NO RETURN at the end.  You may use ansi colors in the file.

@ENDNODE
******************************************************************************
@NODE TT2 "Files-Reverse V1.3 Icon ToolType - Colors"

 @{b}Template: @{ub}Colors=[YES/NO]
  @{b}Example: @{ub}Colors=YES 

 To  make colors in the listings default, set this tooltype to YES.  Colors
 will be used in the file number, (if used), and file information.
 
@ENDNODE
******************************************************************************
@NODE TT3 "Files-Reverse V1.3 Icon ToolType - ShowNewDate"

 @{b}Template: @{ub}ShowNewDate=[YES/NO]
  @{b}Example: @{ub}ShowNewDate=YES 

 To  enable the date-divider graphic, ie what is shown when there is a date
 change  in  the  listing,  set this tooltype to YES.  The text in the file
 "FR-Date.txt"  will  be  utilized  as  the date-divider graphic.  The file
 should  be  ONE  line  long  with  no  tail  return.   To denote where (if
 anyplace) the date should be written, write "@THEDATE".

@ENDNODE
******************************************************************************
@NODE TT4 "Files-Reverse V1.3 Icon ToolType - FileNumbers"

 @{b}Template: @{ub}FileNumbers=[YES/NO]
  @{b}Example: @{ub}FileNumbers=YES 

 If  you  want file-numbers to be shown and want number flagging available,
 set  the  "FileNumbers"  tooltype to YES.  With this option, filenames are
 assigned 1 to 2 digit numbers, which makes for easier file flagging.

@ENDNODE
******************************************************************************
@NODE TT5 "Files-Reverse V1.3 Icon ToolType - NocWhoCompat"

 @{b}Template: @{ub}NocWhoCompat=[YES/NO]
  @{b}Example: @{ub}FileNumbers=YES 

 If  you are using a nocTurne deSign who door (noC-WHO), set "NocWhoCompat"
 to YES.  Files-Reverse usage will be then recognized by the door

@ENDNODE
******************************************************************************
@NODE TT6 "Files-Reverse V1.3 Icon ToolType - Nuker"

 @{b}Template: @{ub}Nuker=[DOORNAME]
  @{b}Example: @{ub}Nuker=NUKE 
 
 Files-Reverse  has  the ability to call a nuker any time during the use of
 the program.  The default door-name called is 'NUKE'.  To change this, set
 the  'Nuker='  tooltype  in the 'FR.x' icon.  The nuker is called with the
 'X' key at the pause prompt.

@ENDNODE
******************************************************************************
@NODE TT7 "Files-Reverse V1.3 Icon ToolType - NukeAccess"

 @{b}Template: @{ub}NukeAccess=[NUMBER]
  @{b}Example: @{ub}NukeAccess=250

 To  set  the  security  level  needed  to access the Nuke feature, set the
 'NukeAccess=' tooltype.

@ENDNODE
******************************************************************************
@NODE TT8 "Files-Reverse V1.3 Icon ToolType - LowMemory"

 @{b}Template: @{ub}LowMemory=[YES/NO]
  @{b}Example: @{ub}LowMemory=NO

 A  Low-Memory  mode is available in FR, which is normally activated in low
 memory  situations.   However to turn this feature on permanently, set the
 "LowMemory"  tooltype to YES.  Benefits to this include 10K of memory used
 at  any  one time (as opposed to memory the size of the directory itself),
 and  faster  startup,  (as  FR does not have to load the whole directory). 
 Side effects include disk accessing during the usage of the program, and a
 subtle  slow  down.

@ENDNODE
*****************************************************************************
@NODE USAGE "Files-Reverse V1.3 - Usage"

 After  typing 'FR' without any arguments from the command line, files from
 the  upload  directory  of  the current conference are displayed newest to
 oldest.    (Please  note:  The  door  name  'FR' should never be altered).
 Several  options are available to the user.  Some of the fundamental usage
 arguments are:


 'FR ?' will bring up information on the program and its usage.

 'FR O'  will  run the door with configurable parameters.  The user will be
 prompted  for  the  date  from  which  the  listing  should  start and the
 directory  to  list.    If  there is more than one directory, the user may
 select from the alternatives.
     
 'FR E'  will  allow  the  user  to  configure  FR   to   his   own  taste.
 Configuration data will be stored in the file "DOORS:noC-FR/fr-users.dat".
     

 When  the  listing  is paused, the user may flag files, abort the listing,
 set the listing to nonstop mode, nuke files, (if he has proper access), or
 continue.   CTRL-C aborts are supported.  Usage is very intuitive, I don't
 think any more detail is neccessary.

@ENDNODE
